/-!
# Simplicity, Step 3: `K` contains every elementary matrix

`simple_kazhdan_sofic_group.tex`, subsection "Simplicity", tex l.241–242 and Step 3, l.299–315:

> We show in three steps that $K=G$. (l.241–242)
>
> The set $J=\{r\in R:e_{pq}(r)\in K\text{ for all }p\ne q\}$ is a two-sided ideal
> by~\eqref{eq:elementary}, since $e_{pq}(r'r)=[e_{pl}(r'),e_{lq}(r)]$ and
> $e_{pq}(rr')=[e_{pl}(r),e_{lq}(r')]$ for $l\notin\{p,q\}$. (l.299–302) It contains $e_V$, so it
> contains every $e_{\xi V}=u_\xi e_V u_\xi^{-1}$. By minimality and compactness finitely many of
> these sets cover $C$, so $1=1-\prod_i(1-e_{\xi_iV})\in J$. (l.303–305) Then $J=R$ and $K=G$.
> (l.305) This proves~(a). (l.305)
>
> For derived topological full groups, Matui showed by a similar argument ... (l.307–309)
> For the ring $\LC(X,\F_2)\rtimes_T\Z$ of Theorem~\ref{thm:main}, simplicity also follows from
> Stepanov's theorem on the normal structure of $\GL_n$~\cite[Theorem~4.4]{Stepanov}: this ring is
> simple~\cite[Corollary~4.6]{ClarkEdie}, and for any $p,q$ in it there are $r,r'$, not both $0$,
> with $pr+qr'=0$, by a dimension count on a tower over one small cylinder. (l.309–315)

Part (a) of `thm:general` (tex l.172–178): for a finitely generated group `Λ` acting minimally and
topologically freely on a Cantor set `C`, with `R = LC(C, F_2) ⋊ Λ` generated by a finite set
`S ∋ 1`, for every `n ≥ 3` the group `EL_n(R)` is an infinite, finitely generated, simple Kazhdan
group.

Proof route:

* `K = G`: the simplicity of `EL_n(LC(Z, F_2) ⋊ Λ)` (`General.isSimpleGroup_clopenGroupCrossedProduct`,
  assembled from Steps 1–3 in the corpus);
* `J` is `Pestov91.SimpleModCentre.levelIdeal`, a two-sided ideal; the printed commutator identities
  are `elGen_commutator`;
* the finite cover is `General.exists_finset_smul_cover`; `∏ (1 - e_{ξV}) = 0`
  (`General.prod_one_sub_charFn_smul_eq_zero`); `1 ∈ J` is
  `General.one_mem_levelIdeal_of_smul_cover` for the covariant pair of the crossed product;
* `1 ∈ J` gives `J = R`; the elementary group is generated by the roots
  (`elementaryGroup_hom_eq_one_of_gens`), so `K = G`;
* part (a): property (T) and infiniteness (`printedGroupCrossedProductPropertyTInfinite`), finite
  generation from property (T) (`KazhdanFiniteGeneration.fg_of_hasKazhdanPropertyT`), simplicity;
* the Stepanov route: `isSimpleRing_R`, `pairDependence_R`, condition (b)
  (`stepanovConditionB_of_pairDependence`), the sandwich theorem
  (`StepanovNormalStructure.sandwich_of_conditionB`), and the resulting simplicity.
-/

namespace GroupApproximation
